From 7e652294032907a6a470a9bed36d1828420da670 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:14:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] U09 review: verse-part letters, and refChapters stops at
 another book

- Both parsers read a part of a verse ("Romans 3:23b", "Luke 22:19b-20")
  as the whole verse. The study guides and Bible notes cite half-verses in
  prose, and U03's essay gate recognizes "3:23b" by shape, so a parse check
  wired into validate-essays.mjs would otherwise fail on it.
- refChapters no longer reads "and 2 Timothy 4:20" as chapter 2 of the
  first book: five catalogue lines ("2 Corinthians 12:7-9 and 2 Timothy
  4:20", "Psalm 90:4 and 2 Peter 3:8", ...) listed their item under the
  wrong chapter (inherited from the old parser).
- A catalogue line's reference is cut where any word or number ends, so
  "Genesis 1:5. The day" or "Genesis 1:5, the day" reads as Genesis 1, as
  the old regex did.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JuCQ8kZ25i9zRwNgk6bh4e
